OAO6SJc6xcVsC","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T14:58:41Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T14:59:08Z","body":"I would argue it's still a UX issue. Closing a tab like that doesn't reset the tab bar scroll position in any browser I've tried. I can see why it does that if you close the currently open scene, but closing with middle click doesn't change scene focus at all.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2976996098/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977164077","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106910#issuecomment-2977164077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106910","id":2977164077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xc-st","user":{"login":"precup","id":709680,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwOTY4MA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/709680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup","html_url":"https://github.com/precup","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/precup/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-16T15:50:11Z","updated_at":"2025-06-16T16:07:42Z","body":"I've tested out every tab based application I can think of on my computer and the results are consistent.\n\nMost programs either don't allow scrolling away from the open tab or don't allow middle click closing. The four I found that do are:\n- Firefox\n- Chrome (with tab scrolling enabled)\n- Visual Studio Code\n- FileZilla\n\nAll four of those programs behave the way I expect and do not teleport me away from what I'm doing. They all behave consistently. Godot is the only odd one out I can find.\n\nEDIT: I realize it's a vertical tab list instead of a horizontal one, but the script editor in Godot itself also doesn't teleport you away. It matches the common behavior, which is helpful for the exact same case: closing lots of old tabs.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2977164077/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2979239675","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/106910#issuecomment-2979239675","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106910","id":2979239675,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6xk5b7","user":{"login":"AdrienUfferte","id":13836669,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEzODM2NjY5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/13836669?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte","html_url":"https://github.com/AdrienUfferte","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdrienUfferte/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-06-17T07:24:57Z","updated_at":"2025-06-17T07:25:55Z","body":"I made some investigations, and it appear you are right and I was wrong. It is indeed a UX issue, and the majority of \"big projects\" have another behaviour.\n\n\n💡 Best UX compromise :\n- ✅ Do not scroll automatically when a tab is closed. If the user has scrolled the list of tabs, it is probably on purpose!\n- 💬 Add a subtle animation or a small indicator (e.g. a dot) on the active tab if it's out of the visible area.\n- 🧭 Bonus: Offer a \"Return to Active Tab\" button on the tab bar (similar to VSCode's \"Reveal Active Tab\").","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2979239675/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"